# SHADOW BOXING

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

Shadow Boxing is a combat-specific movement exercise performed without physical contact to develop technical proficiency, movement efficiency, tactical awareness and neuromuscular coordination.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the highest-value technical exercises due to its versatility, minimal fatigue cost and exceptional transfer to combat performance.

---

# Philosophy

Elite fighters do not use Shadow Boxing merely to warm up.

They use it to refine movement quality.

Every repetition should reinforce efficient mechanics, timing, rhythm, balance and tactical decision-making.

CAS selects Shadow Boxing whenever technical quality is the primary objective.

